,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.03617686965571165,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":25.5,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07598071794791028,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":95.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.009302460624221576,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":61.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.018040663587605643,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":69.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.00733,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.9,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"First Hawaiian, Inc. operates as a bank holding company for First Hawaiian Bank that provides a range of banking products and services to consumer and commercial customers in the United States. It operates in two segments: Retail Banking and Commercial Banking. The company offers various deposit products, including checking, savings, and time deposit accounts, and other deposit accounts. It also provides residential and commercial mortgage loans, home equity lines of credit and loans, automobile loans and leases, secured and unsecured lines of credit, installment loans, small business loans and leases, as well as commercial lease and auto dealer financing services. In addition, the company offers wealth management, personal installment, individual investment and financial planning, insurance protection, trust and estate, private banking, investment management, retirement planning, and credit card and merchant processing services, as well as consumer and commercial credit cards processing services. Further, the company provides commercial and industrial lending, such as auto dealer flooring, commercial real estate lending, and construction lending services. It offers its products through branch, online, and mobile distribution channels. The company was formerly known as BancWest Corporation and changed its name to First Hawaiian, Inc. in April 2016. First Hawaiian, Inc. was founded in 1858 and is headquartered in Honolulu, Hawaii.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert Scott Harrison | Chairman of the Board, President & CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $446K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $154K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["First Hawaiian, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.0B market cap on $881M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $303M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 34 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.4pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 21% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[